      └── generated artifacts
29. What happens to workspace after a build?
It can remain for reuse or be cleaned depending on the Jenkins configuration/pipeline.


Workspace means the folder where Jenkins does the actual work.
If you download a project and work on it, you need a folder:
My Computer
   ↓
project folder
   ↓
application files

Jenkins also needs a folder to work on your application. That folder is called the workspace.


